known_failures: 2 blocking findings, F1 the daemon guard never matches a real opencode.exe serve --service process, F2 the job-root scoping can select a process outside the job root; 3 nonblocking findings, F3 no pid identity check before SIGKILL, F4 the seed export cwd follows the ambient TMPDIR into the repository, F5 the HOME guard compares a constant and never refuses
summary: The credential half holds and the daemon guard does not. The seed export makes one real-HOME call, its value stays on the pipe, the stderr files are mode 600 and removed, and no other real-HOME call form exists. The daemon guard never matches a real opencode.exe serve --service process, because it tests the raw cmdline string, and its job-root scoping compares raw path strings, so it can select a process outside the job root. Both facts are machine-verified on a synthetic process table.
blocking_f1: The daemon guard never matches a real daemon. review-run.sh:420 and judge-run.sh:315 test the raw /proc/<pid>/cmdline string for serve --service. The kernel separates argv entries with NUL, so a real opencode.exe serve --service process holds serve NUL --service. On a synthetic process table, pid 1001 with three argv entries and HOME and cwd inside the job root was not selected, while pid 1002 with the fake one argv0 was selected. The guard cannot stop the stray daemon of the opencode_host_isolation fault. The tests D1, D2, D3 and JD1 pass only because the fake spawns its daemon with exec -a fake-opencode serve --service TAG, a shape no real process has. Fix: join the argv entries before the match and let the fake use three argv entries.
blocking_f2: The job-root scoping can select a process outside the job root. The under helper at review-run.sh:412 and judge-run.sh:307 compares raw path strings. A process whose HOME string is job-root slash dotdot slash outside slash home resolves outside the job root but still matches the prefix, so the guard sends TERM and then KILL to it. On the synthetic table, pid 3001 was selected for the job root. This breaks 4.13o contract item 2 and the plan row 4.13p claim that the guard never touches an outside process. Fix: resolve the HOME and cwd paths before the comparison.
nonblocking_f3: The KILL step has no pid identity check. daemon_pid_alive at review-run.sh:393-400 reads only the state field of /proc/<pid>/stat. If the daemon dies on TERM and the pid is reused inside the 5 s wait, the SIGKILL at review-run.sh:457 and judge-run.sh:352 hits an unrelated process. The pid_max of this host is 4194304, so the risk is low here. Fix: compare the starttime field before the KILL.
nonblocking_f4: The seed export cwd is not guaranteed to sit outside a git repository. provider-credential.sh:159 builds the folder with mktemp -d under the ambient TMPDIR. With TMPDIR set to the repository, the seed cwd became repo slash measure slash runs slash mg-seed-export.Q06KCq, inside the git work tree. The PM condition in proof-real-home-export.txt needs a cwd outside any git repo, because a repo cwd makes the opencode CLI spawn git commands at boot. The S1 and JS1 assertions check only the cwd folder itself, so they cannot see a git ancestor. Fix: use a fixed root outside the repository, or check every ancestor for .git.
nonblocking_f5: The HOME guard compares a constant, so it can never refuse. check_job_home receives the literal FOLDER slash home at provider-credential.sh:87-97, and the runners compare the literal JOB slash home at review-run.sh:662-665 and judge-run.sh:444-449. The invariant holds only because run_opencode hardcodes HOME. The guard never resolves a path, so a symlink at the job home would send the job import into the operator real HOME store without a refusal. An unset or relative HOME is not examined either. Fix: compare the resolved HOME with the resolved job root.
